c2c should always add mcp servers as disabled

Lane: install-supervision, serial after B296 (same worktree). Decision on intent: every NEW c2c MCP server entry c2c writes lands disabled — claude .mcp.json / ~/.claude.json entries get disabled:true; codex [mcp_servers.c2c] gets the disabled flag only if the codex config schema actually supports one (verify; else skip that client and note). Existing entries are never re-disabled (operator choice preserved; idempotent re-runs). Rationale: consistent with init MCP-off-by-default and B300 explicit-activation.

Implemented on fix/B296-B290-install (worktree .worktrees/b296-b290-install): claude .mcp.json + ~/.claude.json entries get "disabled": true when NEWLY added; codex [mcp_servers.c2c] gets enabled = false when newly added — codex schema DOES support the key (per-server enabled, default true; confirmed via official codex config docs). Idempotence: an existing c2c entry is rewritten with the operator disabled/enabled state carried over verbatim, including absent-field-stays-absent (operator enabled). Kimi/opencode writers untouched (out of lane decision scope). Tests: test_c2c_setup_claude (3 new), test_c2c_setup_codex (2 new); RED-first.